@stefansjfw 
Please look at #34557 before merging. Maybe the hashes are wrong. > @stefansjfw Please look at #34557 before merging. Maybe the hashes are wrong.

Checked, hashes are wrong in the release description. Will be updated there as well soon. Thanks

review_comments:
Please add "From {0}" to resex and use it with `string.Fromat()`. In resex we need a comment like `Like "Convert from Unit".`.

And I wondering if we can improve it by having two or three different resex strings containing all subtitle elements and a switch case before `return new Result ...`. The code line looks a bit messy. @htcfreek
This should also be abstracted into another function since it's used in many places, right? Nvm, I added another function for the same thing and called it multiple times. Too have less duplicated code:

Then we need only one `Result` definition where we use the subTitleText variable.

```suggestion
            string unitFromName = GetFromUnitNameString(result);
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(unitFromName))
            {
                    subTitleText = string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, ConvertFromOunce, ounceName) + " - " + string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, CopyToClipboard, result.QuantityInfo.Name);
            }
            else
            {
                    subTitleText = string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, CopyToClipboard, result.QuantityInfo.Name);
            }
```
 ```suggestion
    <value>From {0}</value>
    <comment>Like "Convert from unit".</comment>
```
 @htcfreek Doesn't the name of the field clears that up? But still resolved it. What about `to ounce`? Should return two results too. Plese add second test case. Please name this more general to allow using it later for other units too. Added! Named it `GetUnitNameString`

issue_comments_text:
We could user default time symbol or we may create a new icon form clock and globe. @TobiasSekan
I suggest 
- to have this subtitle: `Current zone time: ... - Time offset: +9:30`
- let's write `+9:30` in the tooltip.
- In which relation is offset calculated? (System time zone or UTC?)
- Allowvto search without + or - to get both time zones (negative and positive). **[Added later by updating comment]** @TobiasSekan 
Does the plugin have a zone for UTC? i like this plugin very much I have seen that I can't take only the first letters of the name of a Time-Zone to match the Time-Zone shortcut (like UTC),

so I will add a separate JSON to match all possible shortcuts and the official cities of the time zones.
I hope i can finished this in the next month (it is a lot of work).

Stay tuned

BTW: What should I do about cities that have more than one Time-Zones? Any Ideas? My opinion is just leverage basic date time shifts.  Time zone stuff is NP hard problem IMO @niels9001 Can you make a light and dark symbol for the timezone plugin? > @niels9001 Can you make a light and dark symbol for the timezone plugin?

Will do! @TobiasSekan do you need anything from us to wrap this up? Sorry for long down time, I will work the next days on this draft to bring it into PR state, happy holidays

@crutkas You can checkout the draft an test the search results and I need a new symbol from @niels9001 @TobiasSekan 

Here's a dark and light version of an icon that should work for this plugin :).
