review_comments:
It makes sense to move the regex as static readonly variable to the top. Line 23 to 25. 

And we should add a comment to describe how the regex works. Something like `"split on every occurence of the delim except if it is enclosed by " and ignore two " as escaped ".`". How could we do that? Since the regex string also consists of the variable `delim`. My bad. Forgot this. Except we can put the fixed part into a variable and use it every time. But I am not sure if that makes sense. Like, we can do it but it won't make any sense. Also, instead of the variable being a `Regex`, it can be a `string`. I think the only benefit would that we don't copy the regex code into multiple places. Because this happens when you do the other points I mentioned in the main discussion of this PR. But it feels a bit strange to split the regex into two parts.

I think only the comment describing the regex makes sense to add. The variable thing makes no sense. I added the variable `CsvDelimSepRegexStr` to signify the body of the Regex, as it was being used in different places. I also added a comment explaining its usage. ```suggestion
                        // A CSV line is valid, if the delimiter occurs equal times in every line compared to the first data line
                        // and if every line contains no or an even count of quotation marks.
```
 ```suggestion
                        if (Regex.Count(line, delim + CsvDelimSepRegexStr) == delimCount && int.IsEvenInteger(line.Count(x => x == '"')))
```

Here we should validate the nunber of quotation marks. ```suggestion
                    // and if the next csv line does not exist or has the same number of occurrences of the delimiter.
```
 Gotcha! I forgot about getting the total `"` count rather than the required ones. Might be a commit mistake. But the second part regarding the quotation marks is missing. Resolved!

```suggestion
        /* NOTE: Experimentation for OOBE is currently turned off on server side. Keeping this code in a comment to allow future experiments.
``` ```suggestion
            // NOTE: Experimentation for OOBE is currently turned off on server side. Keeping this code in a comment to allow future experiments.
``` ```suggestion
                    /* NOTE: Experimentation for OOBE is currently turned off on server side. Keeping this code in a comment to allow future experiments.
```

You don’t “send to” this language would cause the same problem we have now Well then how should we name it? Help me out. I've had my issue open for 12 months now, but if nobody answers...? P.S. nowhere does it say "send to'" It says "To send:"
The new formulation might be clearer than the current one.
@crutkas , what do you think? Press - To send sound intuitive to me and better than what we have now

issue_comments_text:
@microsoft-github-policy-service agree Yep, there's no convention docs here. I think your strings are good, though :)
I like how actually this brings two features. If one wants to have the crosshairs span across all monitors one can just put a very big number into length.Working pretty good and has everything in place.
LGTM! Thank you for the contribution!

review_comments:
nice :)  nit nit nit: Would be nice to have DependentUpon idl file to have it under .idl file in VS Solution Explorer :)  same here this map is not needed anymore, right? `else` block not needed?  Will this part be needed for later use? Just wondering. Does this metadata serve as an initial value? If yes then it should be true nit: missing var name should this be static? 🤔  Sure, we could use it to benchmark performance later on. Is this import needed?  is this needed? not used ? ```suggestion
                        // To test PowerRename uncomment DEBUG_BENCHMARK_100K_ENTRIES define
``` oh yeah, thanks found that 1M is too long to create it's still needed when you disable `recreate_files` - useful for fast iterations. yes, the property is global and exists regardless of the instance, see e.g. https://github.com/microsoft/microsoft-ui-xaml/blob/main/specs/ScrollingControls/ScrollView.md#scrollview-class-1 I don't get it. You already add ROOT_PATH into g_files in line 130. That should be enough right? This else block is not doing anything? ah, sorry, you're right :) this can be removed, right? `listView_ExplorerItems()` can be used insted Q: Is it possible to merge ExplorerItemViewModel and ExplorerItem into one class?   I don't think so, since for virtualization to work we need to adhere to MVVM pattern, i.e. VMs are never virtualized, as opposed to views, which could be recycled etc. `items` not used anywhere? thanks, removed 👍  nit: not needed?

