review_comments:
Does std::filesystem::directory_iterator work well with us deleting entries while it's iterating? perhaps we should move it into a separate thread, e.g. move before

```cpp
        std::thread{ [] {
            PeriodicUpdateWorker();
        } }.detach();
``` It should be fine since similar code was already used in PowerToys.Update to cleanup msi and exe files and I haven't experienced any issues during tests.
From docs: https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/filesystem/directory_iterator
- The iteration order is unspecified, except that each directory entry is visited only once.
- If a file or a directory is deleted or added to the directory tree after the directory iterator has been created, it is unspecified whether the change would be observed through the iterator.

