 Would it be weird to call it "#HEX" and other one "HEX" (to indicate hashtag symbol)?  We should use thte same casing on both. Otherwise I promise you that users ask for the other two combinations (hex, #HEX) too? In this case, why not add `Hex2` without the `#` instead of changing `Hex`?

The reason for this is that users that already have Hex turned on and are using it will get that unexpected behavior change on upgrade. > The reason for this is that users that already have Hex turned on and are using it will get that unexpected behavior change on upgrade.

Already saw a comment of Niels where he anticipated this. Idea was to reach out to people who have it active, but have issues with the `#`. But yes, _unexpected_ changes can be confusing or break habits.. > > The reason for this is that users that already have Hex turned on and are using it will get that unexpected behavior change on upgrade.
> 
> Already saw a comment of Niels where he anticipated this. Idea was to reach out to people who have it active, but have issues with the `#`. But yes, _unexpected_ changes can be confusing or break habits..

The main issue I have here is that there's no need to break habits if we just add a format instead of changing the existing one. @jaimecbernardo @htcfreek @martinchrzan @stefansjfw @Jay-o-Way 

I think we should move everything to lowercase for both HEX formats (like we have for all color formats). It is easier to read, consistent with e.g. web dev best practices and there's no difference for tools.

Additionally - it feels this gets overly complicated. Maybe we should just stick to 1 HEX format: lowercase, without the #. This will work well with all tools, and worst case a user needs to add a # manually. Consider it a solution to a fix :).

My worry is that we get overly complicated formats (I can imagine users will be asking for rgb formats without the 'rgb(' part, like @htcfreek already pointed out) that are super similiar with minor differences. > @jaimecbernardo @htcfreek @martinchrzan @stefansjfw @Jay-o-Way
