 @davidegiacometti 
Can I use the env vars in file or folder paths like `%programdata%\microsoft` as search query? > @davidegiacometti Can I use the env vars in file or folder paths like `%programdata%\microsoft` as search query?

Yes, and this is already supported by the folder plugin since `%programdata%\microsoft` is expanded to `C:\ProgramData\microsoft`.
The aim of the PR is to provide listing and autocomplete for env variables. > > @davidegiacometti Can I use the env vars in file or folder paths like `%programdata%\microsoft` as search query?
> 
> Yes, and this is already supported by the folder plugin since `%programdata%\microsoft` is expanded to `C:\ProgramData\microsoft`.
> The aim of the PR is to provide listing and autocomplete for env variables.

But which variables do you mean then? Things like `%JAVA_HOME%`?

Or have we only add the ability to list the environment variables that are expanded only in the past?

Atm I don't understand the target of this PR. Sory for that. > But which variables do you mean then? Things like `%JAVA_HOME%`?
> 
> Or have we only add the ability to list the environment variables that are expanded only in the past?
> 
> Atm I don't understand the target of this PR. Sory for that.

Yes, search input like `%programdata%\microsoft` was already supported since folder plugin is expanding env vars.
With this PR I have introduced autocomplete:
- Type `%` to have all the env vars listed
- Type `%PRO` and press TAB key to use autocomplete to type `%PROGRAMDATA%` faster
- Once `%PROGRAMDATA%` is selected folder plugin display %PROGRAMDATA% subfoldersLGTM!
