 LGTM! Thank you for the contribution.

There's an issue, however. The code contains a low level keyboard hook listener in C#. We've received issues before on how this creates the system unresponsive under heavy load, since it'll spend lots of time marshalling/unmarshalling C# stuff. This looks like it's essential for the functionality. 
I think it can still go in like this, but disabled by default. I've just added commit for this.
After merging, let's create an issue to code the relevant parts in C++ instead. small typos Tested, works good.

The only UX issue I've encountered is when you hold <kbd>letter</kbd> + <kbd>arrow</kbd> just long enough to trigger the toolbar to launch. In that case, you won't see UI toolbar at all, but the letter will be replaced by what was the last selected there, so it feels a bit clunky. As a future improvement, perhaps we should stopwatch toolbar screen time and don't replace the letter if it didn't get a minimal time threshold. - Added the list for s.

- Suggestion for later enhancement: App exclude list like for other Toys. some missing variants Tested locally, works well. Didn't face any issues.

