can you elaborate, please?  If the .json file has the key `properties` but doesn't have `open_powerlauncher` subkey, or that subkey doesn't have `win`, `alt`, ... as subkeys, an exception will be thrown (and caught). It makes sense to set the shortcut to Alt+Space in that case. As suggested by @ivan100sic , let's refactor the code and move the code, that now is in the "else", out of the try catch.
If `m_hotkey` is not set in the try-catch, we will set it to its default value. Right now, we assume that a valid settings file is either empty({}) or contains `properties.open_powerlauncher` with all modifier keys. It is better to get an error in logs if that structure changes because it will signify potential issues. We do not want to swallow an error. Of course, we should still log the error. Sorry, I misunderstood your suggestion.  done ```suggestion
