the UI needs to be modified to make sure the new option fits properly.

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3206696/112133640-2f6a0a80-8bcc-11eb-8d3e-d73423cb8121.png)
 @darecluval 
the first letter is not processed:

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3206696/112151937-0f454600-8be2-11eb-87a6-f1ec46b7fa3f.png)
 The reason it's lower camel case with the first letter not being capitalized is that's the example provided in the original issue. Confirming it should expect the first word to be capitalized.  @darecluval 
I think the example in the issue is not correct and I also suspect the term camel case has been used incorrectly, since it refers to capitalize terms inside a word (without spaces) see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel_case

From the original issue:
> there isn't really an option for camel case (the first letter of each word capitalized regardless of what the word might be (even if it's 'of', 'and', 'the', etc unlike title case).

I guess the request was for `Capitalization`, not for camel case.
So in your PR change the term `Make Camelcase` to `Make Capitalized` and convert to uppercase the first term as well. @enricogior if that is the only small UX change needed, can we just merge in and do a PR to correct? @crutkas 
there is more work to do beside the UI glitch, not something I want to commit to do since we have large tasks for 0.37. I did push the changes from camel to capitalized. Unfortunately my VM is acting up so I'm flying blind with the math to fix the UI.  #### Misspellings found, please review:


* Capitalizedransform

