 Tested, works well! Very nice and solid work. 
One detail to be polished is that spacing in grid layouts isn't taken into account. 
I created a 4-zones grid without spacing and a priority grid with a default spacing. When I do a quick switch the spacing isn't changed with a layout. The spacing depends on the first (or not quick-switched) assigned layout on the monitor. If the first layout was canvas, it sets 0 spacing to the grid after the switch.

![Image 2021-03-23 at 11 24 10 AM](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8949536/112117621-9687bf00-8bcc-11eb-9e97-6b5cbf67ba67.jpeg)
![Image 2021-03-23 at 11 34 22 AM](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8949536/112117630-97b8ec00-8bcc-11eb-8f77-fe7130914a32.jpeg)


 > spacing in grid layouts isn't taken into account

I think this should be done in another PR, when we reorganize our data schema. It's happening because some of our functions such as `FancyZonesData::SetActiveZoneSet` aren't doing what exactly what they're supposed to, for example, it won't set spacing for the device based on the value stored in the layout. @ivan100sic 
OK let's merge this and then fix the spacing bug.Tested, worked as expected. Nice work!

