``` I would prefer if we define a `RequiredArgumentsQty` and a `RequiredAndOptionalArgumentsQty` and check if `args.Length` is equal to `RequiredAndOptionalArgumentsQty` Let's make sure that this function doesn't throw exceptions, use the `noexcept` operator and if needed, catch possible exceptions.
Same for `save_oobe_opened_state()` Let's log the error. I didn't realize this is a standalone lib, so it is better to log the error in the caller and not catch the exception here. ```suggestion
        const bool openSettings = std::string(lpCmdLine).find("--open-settings") != std::string::npos;

```

```
                    if (args[(int)Arguments.ElevatedStatus] == "true")
                    {
                        IsElevated = true;
