 @crutkas I have fixed build and conflicts with master > #### New misspellings found, please review:
> * Ignorcase

The bot won't complain if this is merged, or you could rebase to after the bot landed and then it won't complain because that error was already fixed. @jsoref, for odd thing is, i can't seem to find the instance of "Ignorcase" @crutkas yeah, it's fixed by this: 618329c7e000f5c1bf45ce3f7c72678e0985305f (in master)

But, this branch was made before that commit was merged, and the spell-checker is checking the branch as is:
https://github.com/davidegiacometti/PowerToys/blob/issue-7336/src/modules/launcher/Plugins/Microsoft.Plugin.Program/Programs/UWPApplication.cs#L296
>                 // Using Ordinal/OrdinalIgnorcase since these are used internally


There's a tension between spell-checking the result of the merge and the work on a PR. It's hard to explain to someone "yes, this thing which is definitely not in your branch isn't your problem, we made a mistake, ignore it". It's slightly easier to explain "yes, this misspelling is in the base of what you worked on, it's already fixed, you can rebase to get the fix or it will otherwise be fixed when it's merged because it's already there".

I hope that almost makes sense. -- There's just a small window where this version of the problem will continue (any PRs from before the spell-checker). Creating a bug, we'll need to update the YML pipeline to remove it from being signed.

