I think you mean 
`x:Uid="PowerLauncher_Appearance_Behavior` Corrected, it should be: Appearance_GroupSettings.

It already exists in the Resources file for other pages. Can you please update to use enums rather than hardcoded strings? [nit] Can you please move these variable declarations to the start of class?  We should use the theme manager initialized during startup. This is to ensure that only a single state for theme is maintained across the program. You can modify `SettingsWatcher` constructor to pass `ThemeManager` initialized in App.xaml.cs. In our current architecture we do not read the settings directly by using settings classes. Instead we use `SettingsWatcher` for this. The usual flow of changes is something like : 
1.  Update the settings.json file from Settings process.
2. These changes will invoke settings watcher.
3. Look for changes in settings watcher and update settings.

My suggestion would be to remove `SettingsUtils` from ThemeManager. Then look for changes in settingswatcher and call `ChangeTheme` function with new value. It would be better to make `System` a seperate entity. In change theme function `currentTheme ` is set to `System`, however it is immediately changed. Ideally, theme should have one to one mapping with system themes. I would suggest to extract 
```
if (WindowsThemeHelper.IsHighContrastEnabled())
                {
                    Theme highContrastBaseType = GetHighContrastBaseType();
                    ChangeTheme(highContrastBaseType);
                }
                else
                {
                    string baseColor = WindowsThemeHelper.GetWindowsBaseColor();
                    ChangeTheme((Theme)Enum.Parse(typeof(Theme), baseColor));
                }
```
into separate function and call this from `SettingsWatcher`, if system default option is selected. Not sure which enum to use since Wox.Plugin.Theme can't be referenced. Should I move it? You can move the `Theme` enum to `common/ManagedCommon`. This would then be accessible by both powerlauncher and settings.  Theme manager should not be disposed here. The theme manager is already disposed by the class that initialized it. Can you please update it ?  [clarification] Why is this required ? Wouldn't it be set when `theme` is Theme.System if we're moving in manage common, we need to test out the installer works here as well.  if we're moving in manage common, we need to test out the installer works here as well.  Already built the MSI and tested installation: ManagedCommon.dll is deployed in `C:\Program Files\PowerToys\modules\launcher` This is required when `theme == System.Theme` because `ChangeTheme` is called again passing the "real system color" but I need to keep `currentTheme = System.Theme`.
Otherwise if user change the system color again, the new color is not detected by the `ThemeManager`.
Required after removing direct access to settings.

