If you remap Win+Ctrl+A->B, when you press Win, Ctrl, A, the OS sees B as being pressed. Then when you release A the OS will no longer see B as being pressed (B key up is sent) . On releasing Ctrl, a key up for B was being sent again at this stage (whereas it wasn't actually required).
We still need to send it in some cases, such as you press Win, Ctrl, A and then release Ctrl. In this case key up needs to be sent for B since we are reverting back to the physical keys. Shouldn't this PR have an associated Issue? > Shouldn't this PR have an associated Issue?

