 Though it seems to be working mostly fine, I've noticed something very odd: sometimes the thumbnail background goes black!!

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/85504/149657114-99674403-cb9e-4c0b-8aaf-46c43c3fc202.png)

For the record, as this is generating transparent images, I made it return `pdwAlpha = WTS_ALPHATYPE.WTSAT_ARGB` instead of `WTS_ALPHATYPE.WTSAT_RGB` (no alpha channel) like the other providers have, but I don't see how this would be causing the problem I am seeing here...

@jaimecbernardo @yuyoyuppe do you have any insight on this? That issue seems to happen inconsistently, I'm trying some things to mitigate it, but this might not be a problem with the extension but an issue in Windows or my drivers...

Anyway, here's a screenshot in dark mode:

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/85504/149658375-26ae9aa1-2914-4260-84c6-aac402c9f52c.png)
 Note: this is taking a dependency on [Helix Toolkit](https://github.com/helix-toolkit/helix-toolkit).

@crutkas if a new full dependency is something one would prefer to avoid, the toolkit is MIT licensed, so there should be no problem to copy in only the required files to make this work.

Having said that, I am **not** advocating for that (copying the classes in) and would prefer to actually take the dependency as it means someone else with correct knowledge is maintaining them! By the way, the only reason I have not added a Preview Handler with this is because Microsoft 3D Viewer already has a really good one... only problem is that it requires the app to be installed AND to open STLs in it by default! > @jaimecbernardo @yuyoyuppe do you have any insight on this?

No insight here. I'm assuming the color is being added by the code you've been using.

Thanks for contributing! I'm going to assign some reviewers. **Please don't merge this yet!!**

I merged `main` branch to main and something is now broken, so I'm trying to figure out what it is... So I traced the issue to ascii based STLs, the HelixToolkit StLReader is failing to parse those after changing the TargetFramework from netcoreapp3.1 to net5.0-windows!

Further tests show that the problem is a `string.StartWith("\0")` check that is done inside HelixTookit, but caused by different behavior between .netcoreapp31 and .net5

Consider the following line of code:

```csharp
"test".StartsWith("\0");
```

The above will return false in .netcoreapp31, but true for .net5 and .net6...

I'm trying to get some further information on why this change of behavior: https://twitter.com/pedrolamas/status/1483769746227146756 The plot thickens! https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/50521#issuecomment-811523668 Moved to draft Today I submitted a [PR](https://github.com/helix-toolkit/helix-toolkit/pull/1700) to fix the .net5 compatibility issue in Helix Toolkit and that was validated, merged and a new release of the toolkit was pushed to NuGet.

I've now updated said NuGet on the project and confirmed that the issue is now properly fixed.

Given this, I'm putting the PR back to ready for review & merge. @pedrolamas looks like sln is conflicted @crutkas merge conflict fixed! 🙂Wow, very cool contribution, thanks a lot! 

Also not sure what could cause the thumbnail to disappear, since Windows has a dedicated cache for them, so once it's there it should stay as long as you don't change the file. The only theory is that provider crashes for some reason on some file changes? LGTM!
Thank you for the contribution!

