Can be a instance class called `Browser.cs` with some static vars var fallback path, name and icon. I noticed that `PluginPair.Update()` (and by extention `SettingsReader.ReadSettings()`) gets called several times in a row which is weird. `ReadSettings()` should only be called when the file watcher detects a change to the settings file > I noticed that `PluginPair.Update()` (and by extention `SettingsReader.ReadSettings()`) gets called several times in a row which is weird. `ReadSettings()` should only be called when the file watcher detects a change to the settings file

My first idea to this: We have many jsons which are written (the one from PT Run and some plugin only ones from wox) and what I don't know is if we trigger all plugins or only the one with changed settings. Or do you mean that one event executes several reloads (which indeed won't make any sense)? The watcher only watches `%localappdata%\Microsoft\PowerToys\PowerToys Run\settings.json`. A single edit to this file will trigger the event handler multiple times (which would cause multiple reloads).

The settings for all PT Run plugins are in this file (e.g. action keyword, global, enabled, additional options..) I don't like idea of having 2 `BrowserInfo.cs` files. There should be one `BrowserInfo.cs` in some common place. e.g. `src/modules/launcher/Plugins/Common`.
I don't expect this will be used by PT Run itself, PluginManager,etc.. so `Plugins/Common` should be fine.
