issue_comments_text:
@crutkas
I've added you a a reviewer, since this PR brings a new git submodule dependency - [`tl::expected`](https://github.com/TartanLlama/expected).

It's a single-header library for handling errors without exceptions, like `std::optional`, but with a customizable error type instead of the `nullopt`. `exptected` has been proposed for C++ standardization for a long time, but didn't make it in time for C++20.  The library is written by a MS employee. It will help with explicit error-handling and reducing the amount of boilerplate. 
